# UI and Design Standard

- The approved homepage on `main` is the visual/UX baseline; do not redesign, restyle, or add interaction spectacle during business/SEO cleanup.
- Prefer legibility, useful hierarchy, responsive layout, native keyboard support, mobile-safe touch targets and reduced-motion behavior.
- Use existing project tokens and components where possible. OKLCH, CSS @property, WebGL and glass effects are options—not mandatory design patterns.
- Test actual 320–390 px mobile layouts and representative desktop widths before claiming polish.
- Distinguish performance measurements from visual preference. No unsupported performance or conversion claims.
